Q. Unable to access server via ssh/RDP, what are the reasons?
Ans :
1. Instance current status - running or not
2. Will check the ec2 Health status is 2/2 or not, if it is 0/2 then there is some issue with aws hardware or if it is 1/2 then check OS
   system logs/instance screen shot.
3. When its 0/2 so we can stop and start the server so that this ec2 instace move from one physical host to another and will have
   the chance it can be 2/2.
4. Need to check ec2 SG that SSH or RDP port is allowed or not.
5. Need to check NACL if SSH or RDP port denied.
6. Check if instace in public or private subnet.
7. Check VPC has the IGW or not.
8. Check route table has proper IGW entry.
9.  In Cloudtrail we can event history- any recent changes happen to the ec2. 

