Q. Please tell your aws archtecture end to end ?
Ans : 
We use a multi-account architecture managed by AWS Organizations. Each environment has its own VPC across multiple AZs. Public subnets host ALB, Bastion, and NAT Gateway, 
while private subnets host application servers in Auto Scaling Groups and RDS databases. Route 53 handles DNS, traffic flows through ALB, and scaling is based on CPU or request count. 
Security is enforced using IAM roles, Security Groups, SCPs, and monitoring is done using CloudWatch and CloudTrail.

